   "id": 616899,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In the <i>Swann v. Charlotte-Mecklenburg Board of Education</i> case (1971), the Supreme Court ruled that",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1174820,
     "content_html": "school busing was a constitutional tool for achieving racial integration"
    },
    {
     "id": 1174819,
     "content_html": "school busing plans could not cross into suburban districts"
    },
    {
     "id": 1174818,
     "content_html": "segregated schools were constitutional as long as they had “equal” resources"
    },
    {
     "id": 1174817,
     "content_html": "school busing to achieve desegregation was unconstitutional"
    }
   ],
